# Port patch, a wish of the project owner (10.11.2026, version 0.99.8; port/docs/whole-program-status.md): the app
# menu's "Aggressive frame skip (saves CPU)". The renderer's Frame skip leaves out a picture the game has built
# already and saves only the GPU's time; here the game itself leaves a picture out while its frames run late
# (runtime/cpu_skip.cpp decides: the frame before took longer than its two fields, at most one in a row, a frame
# over 250 ms does not count, no credit when ahead), so the processor's time for it is saved too (on the PC
# 83-86 % of a frame's work in r103/r105 is drawing).
# The picture is one frame behind the logic (Trans fills the ordering tables, the next frame's Render draws them),
# so a picture left out is a pair:
#   - main.cpp: re4_cpu_skip_decide before Trans (only while the player plays: Rno0 3, two fields a frame, no
#     stopped transform, held picture or sub screen); at the next frame's start re4_cpu_skip_picture: then no
#     Render_before, Render_skip for Render, no cinema bars, DrawOTag, debug log or debug texts (their buffer
#     cleared), Render_done_skip for Render_done and no Render_swap (the VI keeps the picture before).
#   - trans.cpp Trans: no objects and enemies (culling, lights, skinned vertices) for a picture left out; the effects,
#     the effect generators, the ctrl manager, shadows, cloth, filters (rain and snow move in Filter06Trans) and
#     render textures register as always (dropped with the ordering tables). commonScreenMatSub advances the
#     texture animations and scrolls once more for each picture left out before (re4_tex_steps), so they keep
#     their speed. Render_skip: the fog as in Render (it sets the view's far plane the culling uses) and the flags
#     Render leaves.
#   - main_sub.cpp Render_done_skip: no copy, no wait for the GPU; the scenario's C task gets its time slices.
#   - fade.cpp FadeControl: the fades advance in every frame, their quad is not drawn into a picture left out.
# The logic runs as in every frame: checked on the PC with the state trace (RE4_CPU_SKIP_TEST=1, every second
# picture left out: the same trace frame by frame as without).
